<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Calmont Klettersteig and Höhenweg Loop — Complete Calmont Klettersteig and Höhenweg loop</name><desc>The Calmont loop near Bremm begins at the signed Eller junction above the railway bridge. Climb to Galgenlay and follow the complete lower assisted trail west, taking the Amphitrion return spur, to the platform above Bremm church. Retrace the short eastern section to the summit branch and climb to the summit cross. Follow the high ridge past the Roman sanctuary, take the Vier-Seen-Blick return spur, and descend through Galgenlay to Eller. Narrow vineyard paths, ladders and cables require dry conditions, sure-footedness and a head for heights; this is not a continuously protected climbing route. Avoid wet rock, frost, ice and hot midday conditions, carry water and sun protection, and obey current closures. Stay out of cultivated vineyard terraces and do not disturb the sanctuary.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).

